From 29f8f579158d5fab600692202cb6ac722e0835d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ttabouch12 <ttabouch12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:13:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/21] power: supply: sm5705_fuelgauge: add Silicon Mitus
 SM5705 fuel gauge driver

Add a power_supply driver for the voltage-tracking fuel gauge of the
SM5705 companion chip found on Samsung Exynos7870 devices (I2C 0x71).

It reports capacity, voltage, OCV, current, temperature, present,
technology, design charge/voltage (from monitored-battery) and the
status of the charger referenced by power-supplies. When the gauge
reports that it has not been initialised, the battery model (tables and
parameters, taken from the vendor kernel) is loaded from devicetree
properties, following the vendor init sequence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C7LhHWjrzX28CzyNMEnVDk
